      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( x \\) given that \\( y = \\frac{1}{2} x \\) and \\( y = \\frac{1}{5} z \\), with \\( z = 60 \\).\n\nFirst, substitute the value of \\( z \\) into the equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = \\frac{1}{5} z = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 60 = 12. \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( y = 12 \\), we can use the relationship between \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{1}{2} y = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
